    scorers=[MatchScorer(column_map={"expected": "expected_answer"})],
    preprocess_model_input=preprocess,
)

asyncio.run(evaluation.evaluate(my_model))
```

The docs show `column_map` on class-based scorers, so I used one here. The pages I read don't show it on a function-based scorer. The docs also describe an alternative: subclass the scorer and override `score` with the dataset's own column name as the argument, then call `super().score(...)` [S2].

If you use the TypeScript SDK, `preprocess_model_input` isn't available there. Use `columnMapping` on the `Evaluation` instead [S1].
